---
description: Enforces adherence to established documentation best practices, ensuring consistency and quality.
globs: **/*.md
alwaysApply: true
---
- Document solutions thoroughly in markdown.
- Use diagrams to describe high-level architecture and workflows.
- Follow established style guides and conventions.
- Review and revise documentation regularly to keep it up-to-date.
- Get feedback from users and incorporate it into the documentation.
- Provide accurate and up-to-date information on concepts and components.
- Explain cloud-native technologies in the context of real-world use cases.
- Offer best practices for deploying and managing applications.
- Add references to external documentation
- when creating or updating README files for terraform modules,  always use `terraform-docs` to generate information about the terraform resources at the end of the file.
`terraform-docs markdown --output-file README.md .`